parison is cleaner since both Q2 2025 and Q2 2026 are now stated on a consistent (restated) basis, and still shows real underlying growth: total operating income grew 46.7% YoY on the operating-profit line, core banking income (net fee and commission income) was up 22.4% YoY for the half, and impairment charges on loans fell 22.9% YoY as asset quality improved (Stage 3 net ratio 3.3% vs 3.8% at end-2025). Net interest margin held roughly stable at 3.8% (vs 4.1% for FY2025). Bottom line: Q2 2026's strong-looking growth is a mix of genuine core-banking momentum (fee income, lower impairments) and a base effect from Q1 2026 absorbing a one-off fraud charge that Q2 didn't repeat -- treat the QoQ percentage with real caution, the YoY figure is the more comparable one, and the restatement itself is a material governance event independent of this quarter's results.", "source_doc_id": "52054", "source_page": 7, "gaps_note": "Q1 2026 figures used for the QoQ comparison are DERIVED (H1 2026 cumulative minus the separately-disclosed Q2 2026 quarter), not a directly disclosed line -- see notes on the underlying financial_statements rows. Extraction scope for this update is revenue/PAT/EPS/operating profit/margins only (no balance sheet or cash flow detail), per current project scope.", "qoq": [{"metric": "net_margin", "label": "Net Margin", "prior_period_label": "Q1 2026 (quarter ended 31 March 2026, derived)", "prior_value": 0.12730219437078338, "new_period_label": "Q2 2026 (quarter ended 30 June 2026)", "new_value": 0.24583558502073813, "pct_change": 0.9311182044883813, "direction": "improved"}, {"metric": "eps_basic", "label": "EPS (Basic)", "prior_period_label": "Q1 2026 (quarter ended 31 March 2026, derived)", "prior_value": 3.86, "new_period_label": "Q2 2026 (quarter ended 30 June 2026)", "new_value": 7.35, "pct_change": 0.9041450777202072, "direction": "improved"}, {"metric": "profit_after_tax", "label": "Profit After Tax", "prior_period_label": "Q1 2026 (quarter ended 3